\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate verifier error}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{verifier}

\p{We formulate verifier error against an independent success label because a
training reward cannot audit itself. The verifier and evidence interfaces are
in \ref{ftip-0046}--\ref{ftip-0049}. DeepSeek-Prover-V2
\citet{Section 2.3, ``Reinforcement Learning''}{ren2025deepseekproverv2}
supplies a proof-checking instance. The false-accept/false-reject decomposition
is a binary measurement model.}

\p{The rates may vary by task, policy, trajectory length, and adversarial
pressure. A low average error rate need not prevent reward hacking on the
subpopulation favored by optimization.}
